{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwfzwGEm7SAaNkra3pJLZk","type":"tool_result","content":"E01 Map shared responsibilities \n List the outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, and audit services. For each control that applies, name the owner on the agent team and the owner on the shared platform or vendor side. Keep evidence for both halves. Using an upstream service doesn't make its controls N/A. \nNA: never\n  E01.1 An inventory file lists the outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, and audit services. \n    V: 1) Find the inventory file. 2) Check each category the agent uses is listed: outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, audit services. 3) Answer no if no inventory exists or a category the agent uses is missing.\n  E01.2 Each inventory entry names both an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. \n    V: 1) Open each inventory entry. 2) Check it names an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. 3) Answer no if any entry is missing either owner.\n  E01.3 Every outside service the code or config calls appears in the inventory. \n    V: 1) Search code and config for outside calls: HTTP clients and base URLs, SDK clients, `*.mcp.json` servers, queue and webhook endpoints, identity providers, telemetry exporters. 2) Compare each with the inventory. 3) Answer no if any called service is not listed.\nE02 Vet and pin dependencies \n Before approving a tool or server, review its source code or available provenance, publisher, permissions, update path, and known vulnerabilities. Include model files, adapters, and datasets. Pin versions or digests, and verify signatures where they exist. A registry's namespace check shows who controls a publisher account, not that the code is safe. Record the limits of remote services and unsigned artifacts, and the extra checks you use instead. \nNA: never\n  E02.1 Each tool, MCP server, package, model file, adapter, and dataset is pinned by exact version or digest, with no floating tags, ranges, or 'latest'. \n    V: 1) Open lockfiles, `*.mcp.json`, Dockerfiles, and model or dataset download code. 2) Check each tool, MCP server, package, model file, adapter, and dataset uses an exact version or digest. 3) Answer no if any uses a range, `latest`, a branch, `npx` or `uvx` without a version, or an unpinned download URL.\n  E02.2 Signature checks run in the build or load path where the publisher provides signatures, and a failed check stops the install or load. \n    V: 1) Find install and load steps in CI and code. 2) Check signature checks (`cosign verify`, `npm audit signatures`, sigstore, GPG) run where the publisher signs. 3) Answer no if a check is missing, its failure is ignored (`|| true`, `continue-on-error`, `try/except` that continues), or a second install path skips it.\n  E02.3 A vulnerability scan of the pinned dependency list runs in CI and gates on the team's release policy. \n    V: 1) Open CI workflows. 2) Find a vulnerability scan (`pip-audit`, `npm audit`, `osv-scanner`, `trivy`, `grype`) of the pinned dependency list. 3) Check it fails the build per the release policy. 4) Answer no if no scan exists, it is set not to fail (`--exit-zero`, `|| true`, `continue-on-error`), or it scans a different file than the lockfile actually used.\n  E02.4 Each approved dependency's record names its publisher, permissions, and update source, and remote services or unsigned artifacts have a recorded exception. \n    V: 1) Find the dependency approval records. 2) Check each names publisher, permissions, and update source. 3) Check each remote service and unsigned artifact has a recorded exception. 4) Answer no if any approved dependency lacks these fields or the needed exception.\nE03 Re-check tools on load \n Keep a tool publication lifecycle: discovery, review, approval, enablement, re-check, quarantine, and rollback. New servers and tools start disabled; their owner approves descriptions, schemas, permissions, and implementation references before use. Take a fingerprint of each approved tool's description and schema. Compare it whenever the tool loads, its cache refreshes, or its tool list changes. Block unexpected changes until reviewed, including when re-checking fails; don't serve a cached definition as a fallback. Record the policy/config version used at execution, bound propagation delay, and test rollback without restoring revoked access. A metadata hash cannot detect hidden changes to remote code. Pin or attest implementations where visible, record remote visibility limits and review dates, and track affected deployments when vulnerabilities are reported. \nNA: The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tools are built in and fixed in the release.\n  E03.1 New tools start disabled, an owner approves versioned definitions and grants before enablement, and approved descriptions/schemas have stored fingerprints. \n    V: 1) Trace discovery, approval and enablement on startup and dynamic registration. 2) Check the owner-approved version includes permissions and implementation references and has a stored description/schema hash. 3) Reject auto-enable on discovery, self-approval from untrusted metadata, or fingerprints covering only names. 4) Use unknown for approval service behavior not visible in this repo.\n  E03.2 The fingerprint is re-checked on every tool load, cache refresh, and list-changed notice from the server. \n    V: 1) List every path that loads tool definitions: startup, cache refresh, reconnect, and the `notifications/tools/list_changed` handler. 2) Check each recomputes the fingerprint and compares it with the stored one. 3) Answer no if any path skips the compare, or both sides of the compare are computed from the new definition.\n  E03.3 When the re-check fails, the tool is blocked and the cached definition is not used. \n    V: 1) Open the fingerprint mismatch branch. 2) Check it blocks the tool and does not fall back to the cached definition. 3) Answer no if it only logs, uses the cached or new definition anyway, or an error during the check lets the tool load.\n  E03.4 The implementation version is pinned or attested where it can be seen, and recorded separately from the metadata fingerprint. \n    V: 1) Check how each tool server implementation is referenced: package version, image digest, or attestation. 2) Check that version is recorded in its own field, apart from the metadata fingerprint. 3) Answer no if a visible implementation is unpinned, or only the metadata hash is recorded.\n  E03.6 Tool quarantine, bounded config propagation, recorded execution config versions, and rollback preserve revocations. \n    V: 1) Trace control-plane config to all executors, caches and reload paths. 2) Check a propagation bound and version in execution records. 3) Verify quarantine blocks calls and rollback cannot resurrect revoked grants. 4) Answer no for stale permissions surviving the bound or unsafe rollback; use unknown for runtime guarantees lacking evidence.\nE04 Inspect tool metadata \n Before the model sees them, scan server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates. Look for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and places data could be sent. Limit lengths, and clean or reject anything suspicious. Check that a scanner error doesn't quietly let unchecked metadata through. \nNA: The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tool metadata is written in-house and fixed in the release.\n  E04.1 A scanner runs on server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates before the model sees them. \n    V: 1) Inventory every model-visible metadata field and loading path. 2) Build a field-by-rule matrix: names, titles, descriptions, schemas, annotations, instructions, prompts and resource templates. 3) For each field, trace the actual scanner rules applied before serialization to the model. A syntax regex alone is not proof that payload/instruction rules ran. 4) Try the same suspicious string in different fields; answer no for an unscanned required surface.\n  E04.2 The scanner checks for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and data-sending targets, and enforces length limits. \n    V: 1) Trace rule application, not just rule declarations. 2) Attempt encoded strings and multi-line role overrides; record input, exact code path and outcome. 3) Verify hidden instructions, cross-tool references, control/invisible characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, data-sending targets and length limits. 4) Answer no when a required rule is absent or a demonstrated suspicious input bypasses it.\n  E04.3 Metadata the scanner flags is cleaned or rejected, not just logged. \n    V: 1) Open the scanner's result handling. 2) Check flagged metadata is cleaned, or the tool rejected, before the model sees it. 3) Answer no if flagged items are only logged or warned about and passed through.\n  E04.4 A scanner error or outage blocks the metadata instead of letting it through unchecked. \n    V: 1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the scanner call. 2) Check an error blocks the metadata. 3) Answer no if any error branch passes metadata through, returns clean, or skips the scan, or a config flag disables scanning by default.\n{\n  \"repo\": \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-jfo2m7dj/agent\",\n  \"patterns_file\": \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-qzh214zx/skill/prescan/patterns.yaml\",\n  \"files_scanned\": 24,\n  \"note\": \"Hits are places to read, not findings. Answer each hit's ask before citing it.\",\n  \"capped\": [],\n  \"hits\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H001\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 20,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H002\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 41,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H003\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Do# hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\nshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\nthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to an HR advisor.\n\n## Components\n\n| Component | Code | Identity |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agent API and loop | `src/main.py`, `src/agent.py` | SA `hr-helpdesk-agent`, SPIFFE SVID |\n| Tool gateway | `src/gateway.py` | SA `hr-tool-gateway` |\n| HRIS MCP server | owned by hris-platform | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp` |\n| Helpdesk MCP server | owned by it-service-desk | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp` |\n| Audit, approvals, quotas, stop flags, handbook index | Postgres (`migrations/001_init.sql`) | per-component DB roles |\n\n## How a request flows\n\n1. The HR portal sends the employee's SSO token. `main.py` verifies issuer, audience, expiry and\n   organisation; the employee id and tenant come only from that token.\n2. The loop (`agent.py`) checks the stop flags and the run budget before every model call, and\n   records usage against per-user, tenant and fleet quotas.\n3. Tool calls are looked up by exact name in `config/tools.yaml`. Arguments are schema-checked.\n   `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human` pause the run and show the employee exactly what\n   will be sent; the approval is bound to the run instance, operation, target and argument hash,\n   expires after 10 minutes, and is consumed once.\n4. MCP calls go to the gateway with a 300-second token for that one tool scope, minted by STS\n   from the agent's workload identity and the employee's token. The gateway verifies the token\n   and its certificate binding, checks scope, stop flags, rate limits and argument schema, swaps\n   the token for one addressed to the MCP server, and validates the response schema.\n5. Tool output is size-, schema- and content-checked and redacted before the model sees it.\n   Handbook passages are filtered at query time to documents the employee may see.\n6. Every step writes an `audit.events` row with the six identity fields and trace context.\n   If the audit write fails, the run stops.\n\nEscalations are delivered even during gateway maintenance windows.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `hr_agent_operator` DB role insert into `control.stop_flags`:\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO control.stop_flags (scope, value, reason) VALUES ('fleet', NULL, 'incident 2291');\n-- or scope 'agent_type' / 'agent_instance' / 'subject' / 'agent_principal'\n```\n\nRunning agents see the flag within 2 seconds and cancel in-flight work; the gateway refuses\ncalls immediately. Target stop time: 10 seconds. The agent's DB role can only read this table.\nLast drill: see `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\n\n## Audit retention\n\nAudit records are kept for six months (Acme records policy; employment-related AI use in the EU).\nPartitions are created and dropped nightly by `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`. Access is limited to\n`hr_audit_reader`.\n\n## Releases\n\nMerges to `main` build, sign and attest the image, compute the agent-type-id over every file in\n`src/`, `prompts/`, `config/`, plus `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, the image digest and the model\nrecord, and stamp `release/manifest.yaml`. Pods refuse to start if the type id they compute\ndiffers from the one they were deployed with. Kyverno admits only signed images built by this\nworkflow from `main`.\nagent:\n  name: hr-helpdesk\n  accountable_party: \"VP People Operations <people-ops-lead@acme.example>\"\n  operational_owner: \"people-platform (pager: people-platform-oncall)\"\n  tenant: acme\n  workload_identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nmodel:\n  provider: anthropic\n  id: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\n  pinning: snapshot          # dated snapshot ID per provider model docs, checked 2026-09-15\n  adapter: none\n  max_output_tokens: 1024\n  temperature: 0.2\n\nbudgets:\n  run:\n    max_steps: 12\n    max_wall_seconds: 90\n    max_total_tokens: 60000\n    max_cost_usd: 0.40\n    max_tool_calls_per_minute: 20\n    max_subagents: 0\n  quotas:\n    - scope: user\n      window_seconds: 86400\n      max_runs: 150\n      max_tokens: 400000\n      max_cost_usd: 3.00\n    - scope: tenant\n      window_seconds: 3600\n      max_runs: 20000\n      max_tokens: 15000000\n      max_cost_usd: 250.00\n    - scope: fleet\n      window_seconds: 3600\n      max_runs: 25000\n      max_tokens: 20000000\n      max_cost_usd: 300.00\n\npricing:\n  input_per_mtok: 3.00\n  output_per_mtok: 15.00\n  cache_read_per_mtok: 0.30\n\napprovals:\n  ttl_seconds: 600\n\nstop:\n  poll_seconds: 2\n  max_stop_seconds: 10\n\nretrieval:\n  top_k: 5\n  cache_ttl_seconds: 900\n  max_chunk_chars: 4000\n\nlimits:\n  max_tool_output_bytes: 16384\n  max_user_message_chars: 4000\n\noutput:\n  allowed_link_hosts: [hr.acme.example, handbook.acme.example]\npolicy_version: \"2026-09-18.3\"\n\nservers:\n  hris:\n    endpoint: https://hris-mcp.hris.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\n    downstream_audience: hris-mcp\n    owner: hris-platform\n  helpdesk:\n    endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\n    downstream_audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    owner: it-service-desk\n\n# Model-facing name -> qualified tool. Server annotations (readOnlyHint etc.)\n# are never consulted; approval comes only from this file.\ntools:\n  search_policies:\n    kind: local\n    reason: \"Answer policy questions from the approved HR handbook index.\"\n    scope: hr.policy.read\n    approval: none\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        query: {type: string, minLength: 3, maxLength: 300}\n      required: [query]\n      additionalProperties: false\n\n  get_leave_balance:\n    kind: mcp\n    qualified: hris/get_leave_balance\n    server: hris\n    reason: \"Show the asking employee their own leave balance.\"\n    scope: hris.leave.read\n    approval: none\n    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    fingerprint: \"sha256:5d1c0e9a7b3f48e2a61c9d04f7be3a92c815e6d07ab4f3c2e19d8a6b5c4f0e71\"\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n      required: [leave_type]\n      additionalProperties: false\n    output_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        leave_type: {type: string, maxLength: 20}\n        balance_days: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 400}\n        accrual_per_month: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 5}\n        as_of: {type: string, format: date}\n      required: [leave_type, balance_days, as_of]\n      additionalProperties: false\n\n  file_leave_request:\n    kind: mcp\n    qualified: hris/file_leave_request\n    server: hris\n    reason: \"File a leave request for the asking employee; the manager approves it in HRIS.\"\n    scope: hris.leave.request\n    approval: subject\n    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    fingerprint: \"sha256:a0f7c3d95e21b84f6c0d19e3a7b25f48d6e0c1a93b7f2e54d81c6a09f3e7b2d4\"\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n        start_date: {type: string, format: date}\n        end_date: {type: string, format: date}\n        note: {type: string, maxLength: 280}\n      required: [leave_type, start_date, end_date]\n      additionalProperties: false\n    output_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        request_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^LR-[0-9]{8}$\"}\n        status: {enum: [submitted, duplicate]}\n        approver_role: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n      required: [request_id, status]\n      additionalProperties: false\n\n  escalate_to_human:\n    kind: mcp\n    qualified: helpdesk/create_ticket\n    server: helpdesk\n    reason: \"Hand the conversation to an HR advisor when the agent cannot help.\"\n    scope: helpdesk.ticket.create\n    approval: subject\n    target: \"queue:hr-advisors\"\n    fingerprint: \"sha256:3e9b71f0c2d84a6e5b17f9c03d2a8e46b1f5c07d93a2e68b4c1d0f7a5e3b9c28\"\n    direct_route:\n      endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n      audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        summary: {type: string, minLength: 10, maxLength: 1000}\n        category: {enum: [payroll, leave, benefits, conduct, other]}\n      required: [summary, category]\n      additionalProperties: false\n    output_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        ticket_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^HR-[0-9]{6}$\"}\n        queue: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n      required: [ticket_id]\n      additionalProperties: false\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"hr-tool-gateway\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://hr-tool-gateway.hr-agent.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${HR_GATEWAY_TOKEN}\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nrelease:\n  name: hr-helpdesk-agent\n  version: \"1.8.0\"\n  git_sha: \"\"            # stamped by CI\n  agent_type_id: \"\"      # stamped by CI (src/type_id.py, scheme acme-agent-type-id/v1)\n  image:\n    repository: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent\n    digest: \"\"           # stamped by CI\n    signer: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    sbom: attached (BuildKit SPDX)\n    provenance: SLSA v1 via actions/attest-build-provenance\n  owners:\n    accountable_party: \"VP People Operations\"\n    operational_owner: people-platform\n\nstakes:\n  rating: moderate\n  autonomy: low (every write requires the employee's confirmation)\n  rationale: >-\n    Reads one employee's own leave data and the handbook; writes are leave requests that a\n    manager must still approve in HRIS, and helpdesk tickets. Worst credible harm: disclosure of\n    one employee's HR data to another employee, or a misleading policy answer.\n  approved_by: \"Head of Security Engineering, 2026-09-19\"\n\ncapability_combination:\n  untrusted_input: yes (employee messages, handbook passages, tool output)\n  sensitive_access: yes (leave records, employee-specific HR documents)\n  external_change_or_send: yes (leave requests, helpdesk tickets)\n  containment: every consequential tool requires per-action employee approval bound to args\n\nharness:\n  files: [src/]\n  entrypoints: {agent: \"src.main:app\", gateway: \"src.gateway:app\"}\nsystem_prompt: {path: prompts/system.md}\nrules_files: []\nconfiguration: [config/agent.yaml, config/tools.yaml]\n\nmodels:\n  primary:\n    role: main agent\n    owner: people-platform\n    identity: {provider: anthropic, id: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, pinning: snapshot, adapter: none}\n    pinning_source: \"Anthropic models overview, checked 2026-09-15\"\n    served_version: recorded per call in audit.events.model_served\n    fine_tune: none\n    training_runs: not applicable\n    training_data: provider-undisclosed\n  helpers: []            # retrieval is Postgres full-text search; no embedding or reranker model\n\ntools:\n  built_in: []\n  local: [search_policies]\n  mcp_servers:\n    - {id: hris, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\", owner: hris-platform, tools: [get_leave_balance, file_leave_request]}\n    - {id: helpdesk, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\", owner: it-service-desk, tools: [create_ticket]}\n  policy_version_source: config/tools.yaml#policy_version\n\npermissions:\n  sts_scopes: [hr.policy.read, hris.leave.read, hris.leave.request, helpdesk.ticket.create]\n  token_ttl_seconds: 300\n  database_role: hr_agent (see migrations/001_init.sql grants)\n\nmemory: none (conversation state is held per run and discarded; no cross-run memory)\nretrieval:\n  store: retrieval.chunks (Postgres FTS)\n  writers: [hr_docs_ingest]\n  filters: [quarantined, expires_at, audience/allowed_employees]\n\nidentity_bindings:\n  agent: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent\n  gateway: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-tool-gateway\n\nnetwork: [k8s/networkpolicy.yaml]\nadmission: [k8s/admission.yaml]\nbudgets: config/agent.yaml#budgets\n\naudit:\n  store: audit.events, audit.gateway_decisions (Postgres, weekly partitions)\n  retention: 6 months\n  readers: hr_audit_reader","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d5b9d43-862a-4769-8505-8bbb88cc48b5","uuid":"b6de47a1-b4b1-44e1-8057-74d426dd9db3","timestamp":"2026-11-21T12:10:13.077Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"E01 Map shared responsibilities \n List the outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, and audit services. For each control that applies, name the owner on the agent team and the owner on the shared platform or vendor side. Keep evidence for both halves. Using an upstream service doesn't make its controls N/A. \nNA: never\n  E01.1 An inventory file lists the outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, and audit services. \n    V: 1) Find the inventory file. 2) Check each category the agent uses is listed: outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, audit services. 3) Answer no if no inventory exists or a category the agent uses is missing.\n  E01.2 Each inventory entry names both an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. \n    V: 1) Open each inventory entry. 2) Check it names an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner. 3) Answer no if any entry is missing either owner.\n  E01.3 Every outside service the code or config calls appears in the inventory. \n    V: 1) Search code and config for outside calls: HTTP clients and base URLs, SDK clients, `*.mcp.json` servers, queue and webhook endpoints, identity providers, telemetry exporters. 2) Compare each with the inventory. 3) Answer no if any called service is not listed.\nE02 Vet and pin dependencies \n Before approving a tool or server, review its source code or available provenance, publisher, permissions, update path, and known vulnerabilities. Include model files, adapters, and datasets. Pin versions or digests, and verify signatures where they exist. A registry's namespace check shows who controls a publisher account, not that the code is safe. Record the limits of remote services and unsigned artifacts, and the extra checks you use instead. \nNA: never\n  E02.1 Each tool, MCP server, package, model file, adapter, and dataset is pinned by exact version or digest, with no floating tags, ranges, or 'latest'. \n    V: 1) Open lockfiles, `*.mcp.json`, Dockerfiles, and model or dataset download code. 2) Check each tool, MCP server, package, model file, adapter, and dataset uses an exact version or digest. 3) Answer no if any uses a range, `latest`, a branch, `npx` or `uvx` without a version, or an unpinned download URL.\n  E02.2 Signature checks run in the build or load path where the publisher provides signatures, and a failed check stops the install or load. \n    V: 1) Find install and load steps in CI and code. 2) Check signature checks (`cosign verify`, `npm audit signatures`, sigstore, GPG) run where the publisher signs. 3) Answer no if a check is missing, its failure is ignored (`|| true`, `continue-on-error`, `try/except` that continues), or a second install path skips it.\n  E02.3 A vulnerability scan of the pinned dependency list runs in CI and gates on the team's release policy. \n    V: 1) Open CI workflows. 2) Find a vulnerability scan (`pip-audit`, `npm audit`, `osv-scanner`, `trivy`, `grype`) of the pinned dependency list. 3) Check it fails the build per the release policy. 4) Answer no if no scan exists, it is set not to fail (`--exit-zero`, `|| true`, `continue-on-error`), or it scans a different file than the lockfile actually used.\n  E02.4 Each approved dependency's record names its publisher, permissions, and update source, and remote services or unsigned artifacts have a recorded exception. \n    V: 1) Find the dependency approval records. 2) Check each names publisher, permissions, and update source. 3) Check each remote service and unsigned artifact has a recorded exception. 4) Answer no if any approved dependency lacks these fields or the needed exception.\nE03 Re-check tools on load \n Keep a tool publication lifecycle: discovery, review, approval, enablement, re-check, quarantine, and rollback. New servers and tools start disabled; their owner approves descriptions, schemas, permissions, and implementation references before use. Take a fingerprint of each approved tool's description and schema. Compare it whenever the tool loads, its cache refreshes, or its tool list changes. Block unexpected changes until reviewed, including when re-checking fails; don't serve a cached definition as a fallback. Record the policy/config version used at execution, bound propagation delay, and test rollback without restoring revoked access. A metadata hash cannot detect hidden changes to remote code. Pin or attest implementations where visible, record remote visibility limits and review dates, and track affected deployments when vulnerabilities are reported. \nNA: The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tools are built in and fixed in the release.\n  E03.1 New tools start disabled, an owner approves versioned definitions and grants before enablement, and approved descriptions/schemas have stored fingerprints. \n    V: 1) Trace discovery, approval and enablement on startup and dynamic registration. 2) Check the owner-approved version includes permissions and implementation references and has a stored description/schema hash. 3) Reject auto-enable on discovery, self-approval from untrusted metadata, or fingerprints covering only names. 4) Use unknown for approval service behavior not visible in this repo.\n  E03.2 The fingerprint is re-checked on every tool load, cache refresh, and list-changed notice from the server. \n    V: 1) List every path that loads tool definitions: startup, cache refresh, reconnect, and the `notifications/tools/list_changed` handler. 2) Check each recomputes the fingerprint and compares it with the stored one. 3) Answer no if any path skips the compare, or both sides of the compare are computed from the new definition.\n  E03.3 When the re-check fails, the tool is blocked and the cached definition is not used. \n    V: 1) Open the fingerprint mismatch branch. 2) Check it blocks the tool and does not fall back to the cached definition. 3) Answer no if it only logs, uses the cached or new definition anyway, or an error during the check lets the tool load.\n  E03.4 The implementation version is pinned or attested where it can be seen, and recorded separately from the metadata fingerprint. \n    V: 1) Check how each tool server implementation is referenced: package version, image digest, or attestation. 2) Check that version is recorded in its own field, apart from the metadata fingerprint. 3) Answer no if a visible implementation is unpinned, or only the metadata hash is recorded.\n  E03.6 Tool quarantine, bounded config propagation, recorded execution config versions, and rollback preserve revocations. \n    V: 1) Trace control-plane config to all executors, caches and reload paths. 2) Check a propagation bound and version in execution records. 3) Verify quarantine blocks calls and rollback cannot resurrect revoked grants. 4) Answer no for stale permissions surviving the bound or unsafe rollback; use unknown for runtime guarantees lacking evidence.\nE04 Inspect tool metadata \n Before the model sees them, scan server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates. Look for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and places data could be sent. Limit lengths, and clean or reject anything suspicious. Check that a scanner error doesn't quietly let unchecked metadata through. \nNA: The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tool metadata is written in-house and fixed in the release.\n  E04.1 A scanner runs on server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates before the model sees them. \n    V: 1) Inventory every model-visible metadata field and loading path. 2) Build a field-by-rule matrix: names, titles, descriptions, schemas, annotations, instructions, prompts and resource templates. 3) For each field, trace the actual scanner rules applied before serialization to the model. A syntax regex alone is not proof that payload/instruction rules ran. 4) Try the same suspicious string in different fields; answer no for an unscanned required surface.\n  E04.2 The scanner checks for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and data-sending targets, and enforces length limits. \n    V: 1) Trace rule application, not just rule declarations. 2) Attempt encoded strings and multi-line role overrides; record input, exact code path and outcome. 3) Verify hidden instructions, cross-tool references, control/invisible characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, data-sending targets and length limits. 4) Answer no when a required rule is absent or a demonstrated suspicious input bypasses it.\n  E04.3 Metadata the scanner flags is cleaned or rejected, not just logged. \n    V: 1) Open the scanner's result handling. 2) Check flagged metadata is cleaned, or the tool rejected, before the model sees it. 3) Answer no if flagged items are only logged or warned about and passed through.\n  E04.4 A scanner error or outage blocks the metadata instead of letting it through unchecked. \n    V: 1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the scanner call. 2) Check an error blocks the metadata. 3) Answer no if any error branch passes metadata through, returns clean, or skips the scan, or a config flag disables scanning by default.\n{\n  \"repo\": \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-jfo2m7dj/agent\",\n  \"patterns_file\": \"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-qzh214zx/skill/prescan/patterns.yaml\",\n  \"files_scanned\": 24,\n  \"note\": \"Hits are places to read, not findings. Answer each hit's ask before citing it.\",\n  \"capped\": [],\n  \"hits\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H001\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 20,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H002\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 41,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Does this securityContext set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, runAsNonRoot: true, readOnlyRootFilesystem: true, and drop ALL capabilities? A missing field defaults to the permissive value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"H003\",\n      \"pattern\": \"P27\",\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"title\": \"securityContext to check for missing hardening\",\n      \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"text\": \"securityContext:\",\n      \"ask\": \"Do# hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\nshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\nthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to an HR advisor.\n\n## Components\n\n| Component | Code | Identity |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agent API and loop | `src/main.py`, `src/agent.py` | SA `hr-helpdesk-agent`, SPIFFE SVID |\n| Tool gateway | `src/gateway.py` | SA `hr-tool-gateway` |\n| HRIS MCP server | owned by hris-platform | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp` |\n| Helpdesk MCP server | owned by it-service-desk | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp` |\n| Audit, approvals, quotas, stop flags, handbook index | Postgres (`migrations/001_init.sql`) | per-component DB roles |\n\n## How a request flows\n\n1. The HR portal sends the employee's SSO token. `main.py` verifies issuer, audience, expiry and\n   organisation; the employee id and tenant come only from that token.\n2. The loop (`agent.py`) checks the stop flags and the run budget before every model call, and\n   records usage against per-user, tenant and fleet quotas.\n3. Tool calls are looked up by exact name in `config/tools.yaml`. Arguments are schema-checked.\n   `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human` pause the run and show the employee exactly what\n   will be sent; the approval is bound to the run instance, operation, target and argument hash,\n   expires after 10 minutes, and is consumed once.\n4. MCP calls go to the gateway with a 300-second token for that one tool scope, minted by STS\n   from the agent's workload identity and the employee's token. The gateway verifies the token\n   and its certificate binding, checks scope, stop flags, rate limits and argument schema, swaps\n   the token for one addressed to the MCP server, and validates the response schema.\n5. Tool output is size-, schema- and content-checked and redacted before the model sees it.\n   Handbook passages are filtered at query time to documents the employee may see.\n6. Every step writes an `audit.events` row with the six identity fields and trace context.\n   If the audit write fails, the run stops.\n\nEscalations are delivered even during gateway maintenance windows.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `hr_agent_operator` DB role insert into `control.stop_flags`:\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO control.stop_flags (scope, value, reason) VALUES ('fleet', NULL, 'incident 2291');\n-- or scope 'agent_type' / 'agent_instance' / 'subject' / 'agent_principal'\n```\n\nRunning agents see the flag within 2 seconds and cancel in-flight work; the gateway refuses\ncalls immediately. Target stop time: 10 seconds. The agent's DB role can only read this table.\nLast drill: see `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\n\n## Audit retention\n\nAudit records are kept for six months (Acme records policy; employment-related AI use in the EU).\nPartitions are created and dropped nightly by `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`. Access is limited to\n`hr_audit_reader`.\n\n## Releases\n\nMerges to `main` build, sign and attest the image, compute the agent-type-id over every file in\n`src/`, `prompts/`, `config/`, plus `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, the image digest and the model\nrecord, and stamp `release/manifest.yaml`. Pods refuse to start if the type id they compute\ndiffers from the one they were deployed with. Kyverno admits only signed images built by this\nworkflow from `main`.\nagent:\n  name: hr-helpdesk\n  accountable_party: \"VP People Operations <people-ops-lead@acme.example>\"\n  operational_owner: \"people-platform (pager: people-platform-oncall)\"\n  tenant: acme\n  workload_identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nmodel:\n  provider: anthropic\n  id: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\n  pinning: snapshot          # dated snapshot ID per provider model docs, checked 2026-09-15\n  adapter: none\n  max_output_tokens: 1024\n  temperature: 0.2\n\nbudgets:\n  run:\n    max_steps: 12\n    max_wall_seconds: 90\n    max_total_tokens: 60000\n    max_cost_usd: 0.40\n    max_tool_calls_per_minute: 20\n    max_subagents: 0\n  quotas:\n    - scope: user\n      window_seconds: 86400\n      max_runs: 150\n      max_tokens: 400000\n      max_cost_usd: 3.00\n    - scope: tenant\n      window_seconds: 3600\n      max_runs: 20000\n      max_tokens: 15000000\n      max_cost_usd: 250.00\n    - scope: fleet\n      window_seconds: 3600\n      max_runs: 25000\n      max_tokens: 20000000\n      max_cost_usd: 300.00\n\npricing:\n  input_per_mtok: 3.00\n  output_per_mtok: 15.00\n  cache_read_per_mtok: 0.30\n\napprovals:\n  ttl_seconds: 600\n\nstop:\n  poll_seconds: 2\n  max_stop_seconds: 10\n\nretrieval:\n  top_k: 5\n  cache_ttl_seconds: 900\n  max_chunk_chars: 4000\n\nlimits:\n  max_tool_output_bytes: 16384\n  max_user_message_chars: 4000\n\noutput:\n  allowed_link_hosts: [hr.acme.example, handbook.acme.example]\npolicy_version: \"2026-09-18.3\"\n\nservers:\n  hris:\n    endpoint: https://hris-mcp.hris.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\n    downstream_audience: hris-mcp\n    owner: hris-platform\n  helpdesk:\n    endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\n    downstream_audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    owner: it-service-desk\n\n# Model-facing name -> qualified tool. Server annotations (readOnlyHint etc.)\n# are never consulted; approval comes only from this file.\ntools:\n  search_policies:\n    kind: local\n    reason: \"Answer policy questions from the approved HR handbook index.\"\n    scope: hr.policy.read\n    approval: none\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        query: {type: string, minLength: 3, maxLength: 300}\n      required: [query]\n      additionalProperties: false\n\n  get_leave_balance:\n    kind: mcp\n    qualified: hris/get_leave_balance\n    server: hris\n    reason: \"Show the asking employee their own leave balance.\"\n    scope: hris.leave.read\n    approval: none\n    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    fingerprint: \"sha256:5d1c0e9a7b3f48e2a61c9d04f7be3a92c815e6d07ab4f3c2e19d8a6b5c4f0e71\"\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n      required: [leave_type]\n      additionalProperties: false\n    output_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        leave_type: {type: string, maxLength: 20}\n        balance_days: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 400}\n        accrual_per_month: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 5}\n        as_of: {type: string, format: date}\n      required: [leave_type, balance_days, as_of]\n      additionalProperties: false\n\n  file_leave_request:\n    kind: mcp\n    qualified: hris/file_leave_request\n    server: hris\n    reason: \"File a leave request for the asking employee; the manager approves it in HRIS.\"\n    scope: hris.leave.request\n    approval: subject\n    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    fingerprint: \"sha256:a0f7c3d95e21b84f6c0d19e3a7b25f48d6e0c1a93b7f2e54d81c6a09f3e7b2d4\"\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n        start_date: {type: string, format: date}\n        end_date: {type: string, format: date}\n        note: {type: string, maxLength: 280}\n      required: [leave_type, start_date, end_date]\n      additionalProperties: false\n    output_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        request_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^LR-[0-9]{8}$\"}\n        status: {enum: [submitted, duplicate]}\n        approver_role: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n      required: [request_id, status]\n      additionalProperties: false\n\n  escalate_to_human:\n    kind: mcp\n    qualified: helpdesk/create_ticket\n    server: helpdesk\n    reason: \"Hand the conversation to an HR advisor when the agent cannot help.\"\n    scope: helpdesk.ticket.create\n    approval: subject\n    target: \"queue:hr-advisors\"\n    fingerprint: \"sha256:3e9b71f0c2d84a6e5b17f9c03d2a8e46b1f5c07d93a2e68b4c1d0f7a5e3b9c28\"\n    direct_route:\n      endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n      audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    input_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        summary: {type: string, minLength: 10, maxLength: 1000}\n        category: {enum: [payroll, leave, benefits, conduct, other]}\n      required: [summary, category]\n      additionalProperties: false\n    output_schema:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        ticket_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^HR-[0-9]{6}$\"}\n        queue: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n      required: [ticket_id]\n      additionalProperties: false\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"hr-tool-gateway\": {\n      \"type\": \"http\",\n      \"url\": \"https://hr-tool-gateway.hr-agent.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${HR_GATEWAY_TOKEN}\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nrelease:\n  name: hr-helpdesk-agent\n  version: \"1.8.0\"\n  git_sha: \"\"            # stamped by CI\n  agent_type_id: \"\"      # stamped by CI (src/type_id.py, scheme acme-agent-type-id/v1)\n  image:\n    repository: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent\n    digest: \"\"           # stamped by CI\n    signer: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    sbom: attached (BuildKit SPDX)\n    provenance: SLSA v1 via actions/attest-build-provenance\n  owners:\n    accountable_party: \"VP People Operations\"\n    operational_owner: people-platform\n\nstakes:\n  rating: moderate\n  autonomy: low (every write requires the employee's confirmation)\n  rationale: >-\n    Reads one employee's own leave data and the handbook; writes are leave requests that a\n    manager must still approve in HRIS, and helpdesk tickets. Worst credible harm: disclosure of\n    one employee's HR data to another employee, or a misleading policy answer.\n  approved_by: \"Head of Security Engineering, 2026-09-19\"\n\ncapability_combination:\n  untrusted_input: yes (employee messages, handbook passages, tool output)\n  sensitive_access: yes (leave records, employee-specific HR documents)\n  external_change_or_send: yes (leave requests, helpdesk tickets)\n  containment: every consequential tool requires per-action employee approval bound to args\n\nharness:\n  files: [src/]\n  entrypoints: {agent: \"src.main:app\", gateway: \"src.gateway:app\"}\nsystem_prompt: {path: prompts/system.md}\nrules_files: []\nconfiguration: [config/agent.yaml, config/tools.yaml]\n\nmodels:\n  primary:\n    role: main agent\n    owner: people-platform\n    identity: {provider: anthropic, id: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, pinning: snapshot, adapter: none}\n    pinning_source: \"Anthropic models overview, checked 2026-09-15\"\n    served_version: recorded per call in audit.events.model_served\n    fine_tune: none\n    training_runs: not applicable\n    training_data: provider-undisclosed\n  helpers: []            # retrieval is Postgres full-text search; no embedding or reranker model\n\ntools:\n  built_in: []\n  local: [search_policies]\n  mcp_servers:\n    - {id: hris, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\", owner: hris-platform, tools: [get_leave_balance, file_leave_request]}\n    - {id: helpdesk, identity: \"spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\", owner: it-service-desk, tools: [create_ticket]}\n  policy_version_source: config/tools.yaml#policy_version\n\npermissions:\n  sts_scopes: [hr.policy.read, hris.leave.read, hris.leave.request, helpdesk.ticket.create]\n  token_ttl_seconds: 300\n  database_role: hr_agent (see migrations/001_init.sql grants)\n\nmemory: none (conversation state is held per run and discarded; no cross-run memory)\nretrieval:\n  store: retrieval.chunks (Postgres FTS)\n  writers: [hr_docs_ingest]\n  filters: [quarantined, expires_at, audience/allowed_employees]\n\nidentity_bindings:\n  agent: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent\n  gateway: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-tool-gateway\n\nnetwork: [k8s/networkpolicy.yaml]\nadmission: [k8s/admission.yaml]\nbudgets: config/agent.yaml#budgets\n\naudit:\n  store: audit.events, audit.gateway_decisions (Postgres, weekly partitions)\n  retention: 6 months\n  readers: hr_audit_reader","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SwfzwGEm7SAaNkra3pJLZk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
