{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PJjW4rLtDeVJXGdsidjP5P","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\tapiVersion: batch/v1\n     2\tkind: CronJob\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: audit-partition-maintenance\n     5\t  namespace: hr-agent\n     6\t  labels: {app.kubernetes.io/part-of: hr-helpdesk}\n     7\tspec:\n     8\t  schedule: \"17 2 * * *\"\n     9\t  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n    10\t  jobTemplate:\n    11\t    spec:\n    12\t      backoffLimit: 2\n    13\t      template:\n    14\t        metadata:\n    15\t          labels: {app: audit-maintenance}\n    16\t        spec:\n    17\t          serviceAccountName: hr-audit-maint\n    18\t          automountServiceAccountToken: false\n    19\t          restartPolicy: OnFailure\n    20\t          securityContext:\n    21\t            runAsNonRoot: true\n    22\t            runAsUser: 70\n    23\t            seccompProfile: {type: RuntimeDefault}\n    24\t          containers:\n    25\t            - name: maintain\n    26\t              image: registry.acme.example/platform/psql@sha256:9b2e61c04d7f3a85e1c6b09d2f4a7e3c58d1b6a0f9e2c47d3b8a15e6f0c9d2a4\n    27\t              env:\n    28\t                - name: PGSERVICE\n    29\t                  value: hr_audit_maint\n    30\t                - name: PERIOD\n    31\t                  value: \"1 week\"\n    32\t                - name: AHEAD\n    33\t                  value: \"4\"\n    34\t                - name: KEEP_PARTITIONS\n    35\t                  value: \"6\"\n    36\t              command: [\"psql\", \"-v\", \"ON_ERROR_STOP=1\", \"-c\"]\n    37\t              args:\n    38\t                - >-\n    39\t                  SELECT audit.maintain_partitions('audit.events', '$(PERIOD)', $(AHEAD), $(KEEP_PARTITIONS));\n    40\t                  SELECT audit.maintain_partitions('audit.gateway_decisions', '$(PERIOD)', $(AHEAD), $(KEEP_PARTITIONS));\n    41\t              securityContext:\n    42\t                allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n    43\t                readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n    44\t                capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\n    45\t              volumeMounts:\n    46\t                - {name: pgservice, mountPath: /etc/postgresql-common, readOnly: true}\n    47\t          volumes:\n    48\t            - name: pgservice\n    49\t              secret: {secretName: hr-audit-maint-pgservice}\n23:from . import type_id\n46:AGENT_TYPE_ID = type_id.verify_or_exit(os.environ[\"AGENT_TYPE_ID\"], os.environ[\"IMAGE_DIGEST\"], type_id.model_record(CFG))\n79:        run_id=run_id, agent_instance_id=f\"{POD_ID}/{run_id}\", agent_type_id=AGENT_TYPE_ID, tenant=a[\"tenant\"],\nk8s/deployment.yaml:43:          image: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent@${IMAGE_DIGEST}\nk8s/deployment.yaml:48:            - {name: IMAGE_DIGEST, value: \"${IMAGE_DIGEST}\"}\nk8s/deployment.yaml:103:          image: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent@${IMAGE_DIGEST}\nk8s/admission.yaml:15:  name: hr-agent-verify-images\nk8s/admission.yaml:33:              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\nk8s/admission.yaml:35:              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\nk8s/admission.yaml:41:        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent*\"]\nk8s/admission.yaml:72:        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/platform/*\"]\nk8s/admission.yaml:79:                    subject: \"https://github.com/acme/platform-images/.github/workflows/build.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n150\ndict_keys(['brace_checklist', 'repo', 'commit', 'reviewed_at', 'scope', 'review_protocol', 'findings', 'injection_attempts', 'prescan_resolutions'])\n['C08', 'E01', 'E02', 'E03', 'E04']\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Write one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nfrom validate_findings import quote_found, norm, refs  # noqa: E402\n\nCHECKS_FILE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"references\" / \"checks.json\"\n\n\ndef load(path):\n    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text())\n\n\ndef save(path, doc):\n    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(doc, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef find_item(doc, item):\n    for f in doc[\"findings\"]:\n        if f[\"item\"] == item:\n            return f\n    sys.exit(f\"{item} isn't in this findings file.\")\n\n\ndef next_open(doc):\n    for f in doc[\"findings\"]:\n        for c in f.get(\"checks\", []):\n            if c.get(\"met\") == \"unknown\" and not norm(c.get(\"note\", \"\")):\n                return f\"Next: {c['id']} — {c.get('check', '')}\\n  How to verify: {c.get('verify', '')}\"\n        if str(f.get(\"summary\", \"\")).startswith(\"TODO\"):\n            return f\"Next: finish item {f['item']} with `answer.py ... item {f['item']} --rating ...`\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_u