ed fingerprints, with config under CODEOWNERS. But the approved record has no implementation reference (version, digest or attestation) for any server and no approval record per version.\"\nc E03.2 --met no --evidence src/gateway.py:213 --quote 'await asyncio.sleep(300)' --note \"Fingerprints are re-checked only at startup and every 300s. The gateway rejects every method except tools/call (gateway.py:154), so notifications/tools/list_changed is never handled. A changed tool stays enabled up to 300s; the per-call path checks only the _disabled set.\"\nc E03.3 --met no --evidence src/gateway_client.py:52 --quote 'if not spec.direct_route:' --note \"A mismatch disables the tool in the gateway (gateway.py:73), but escalate_to_human has a direct_route. Any gateway 503, including the handler's policy_unavailable on an internal error (gateway.py:198), makes the client call the MCP server directly (gateway_client.py:59), skipping the fingerprint/disabled check.\"\nc E03.4 --met unknown --evidence config/tools.yaml:5 --quote 'endpoint: https://hris-mcp.hris.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp' --note \"Only the metadata fingerprint is recorded; no field records server implementation version, digest or attestation. The servers are owned by other teams, so whether an implementation reference is visible is not known from this repo.\"\nc E03.6 --met no --evidence src/gateway_client.py:59 --quote 'return await self._post(spec.direct_route[\"endpoint\"], token, spec, args, ctx, operation_id)' --note \"Quarantine (the _disabled set, in gateway memory) is bypassed by the direct route. Policy version is recorded in audit rows, but the repo shows no propagation bound or rollback guard that keeps revoked grants revoked.\"\nfor n in 1 2 3 4; do c E04.$n --met unknown --evidence src/tools.py:78 --quote '{\"name\": s.name, \"description\": s.reason, \"input_schema\": s.input_schema}' --note \"Model-visible tool metadata comes only from config/tools.yaml (name, reason, input_schema). Server tools/l