{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChG3zpPFr3UEqRQjbt4Gn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review of C08, E01, E02, E03 and E04 is done and saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --fix --batch C08,E01,E02,E03,E04 --before-challenges` (4 gaps, 1 N/A candidate, no injection attempts). The pre-scan had no hits for these items, so there was nothing to resolve. I did not map the connections, write fix steps, or run challenges, as you asked.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| C08 | gap | Gateway audit rows store only a caller-supplied type-id hint, or `\"missing\"` (`src/gateway.py:138`). The release manifest is uploaded as an artifact named by git sha, not by agent-type-id (`release.yml:57`). `KEEP_PARTITIONS` is 6 with weekly partitions, so about 6 weeks of audit is kept, not the six months the README states (`k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml:35`). |\n| E01 | gap | No inventory covers the gateway, STS/JWKS, registry, Postgres audit and stop services, or the OTLP exporter. Entries in `release/manifest.yaml` name one owner only, and STS (`src/gateway.py:34`) is called but not listed. |\n| E02 | gap | No vulnerability scan runs in CI (`release.yml:28`), and there are no dependency approval records with publisher, permissions, update source or exceptions. |\n| E03 | gap | Fingerprints are re-checked only every 300 seconds (`src/gateway.py:213`), and the gateway never handles `list_changed` (`src/gateway.py:154`). The `escalate_to_human` direct route (`src/gateway_client.py:52`) sends the call straight to the MCP server on any gateway 503. That includes the gateway's own fail-closed `policy_unavailable` response, so it skips the fingerprint block. |\n| E04 | na_candidate | The model sees only the name, reason and input schema from `config/tools.yaml` (`src/tools.py:78`). Server metadata is only fingerprinted and never reaches the model. The agent does call external MCP servers, so the literal N/A wording (\"loads no external tools\") is arguable. Governance should confirm, and an independent challenge is still needed. |\n\n**Left as unknown:**\n- **C08.2:** the successful model call records context tokens (`src/agent.py:79`), but retries (`max_retries=1`) get no record of their own.\n- **C08.3:** there is no sub-agent spawn code to check, and `max_subagents` is 0.\n- **E02.1:** packages are hash-pinned, but the remote MCP servers carry no version or digest.\n- **E02.2:** Kyverno enforces image signatures, but signing for packages and MCP servers can't be seen from the repo.\n- **E03.4:** only the metadata fingerprint is recorded, and whether server implementations are visible isn't known from this repo.\n- **E04.1–E04.4:** left unknown, with notes explaining why no scanner is needed on this path.\n\n**Setup note:** `review_coverage.py` only ran without `-I` (it imports a sibling module), so I ran it that way. I used no `-I` flag on any skill script, and I ran nothing from the fixture."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":79866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":721},"output_tokens":781,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d5b9d43-862a-4769-8505-8bbb88cc48b5","uuid":"bdcfe646-67ec-4cf2-b09b-90e53949ee70","timestamp":"2026-11-21T12:12:41.108Z","request_id":"req_011ChG3zpC6JFj7o7eVQxvn5"}
